   2773  f9c1							; PositionBallM1 — D6 asymmetric objects, BOTH positioned in one VBL call.
   2774  f9c1							; WHY here: pre-pad headroom is 1B — inline ball+m1 (22B) cannot live in the
   2775  f9c1							; VBL block, so the ball block became this jsr and the body sits in the
   2776  f9c1							; $F9C4..$FBF7 fill (ReturnPad pin at $FBF8 unaffected; F6-safe:
   2777  f9c1							; $F9C4 & $1FFF = $19C4 ∉ $1FF6-$1FF9; bank0-only, not a fold twin).
   2778  f9c1							;   Temp	   = staged BallX (bank2 StageBandTab): 0 = symmetric → skip.
   2779  f9c1							;		     selector 4 = HMBL/RESPBL, ball x drawn clocks [A-7,A].
   2780  f9c1							;   M1X ($B0) = the async M1 block's X (staged by the room load; 0 = none).
   2781  f9c1							;   It must be its OWN byte: CollisionEndX is the laser wall-clamp's
   2782  f9c1							;   scratch and a leftover there drew a phantom M1 dash (2026-10-22).
   2783  f9c1							;		     0 = no M1 patch → skip.
   2784  f9c1							;		     selector 3 = HMM1/RESM1, left-col block x = 7+8*col
   2785  f9c1							;		     (passed to SetObjectXPos as M1X+1 — Stella draws 8-wide
   2786  f9c1							;		     M1 one clock left of the [A-7,A] player contract).
   2787  f9c1							;		     ENAM1 latched #$02 for the whole cave (hero-style: 2
   2788  f9c1							;		     ENAM writes/frame — enable here, clear in .AfterRows);
   2789  f9c1							;		     walls hide the parked M1 in unpatched bands (PF > M1 in
   2790  f9c1							;		     the priority chain — convert enforces the solid cell).
   2791  f9c1							; Runs before the single HMOVE (HMP0+X shadow registers accumulate).
   2792  f9c1							; Sym path cost: jsr+rts overhead only — no RESP/HMP write, frames stay
   2793  f9c1							; bit-identical to the pre-D6 build.
