   3815  fe14							; ==============================================================================
   3816  fe14							; Phase 5 — second GRP1 object (no flicker). TIA has one GRP1 sprite, so two
   3817  fe14							; objects in a room used to alternate frames (30 Hz flicker each). When they
   3818  fe14							; live in DIFFERENT cave bands each can be drawn on ALL of its scanlines: the
   3819  fe14							; band's setup swaps the live trio (ObjBase/ObjTop/ActiveObjectX) for slot 1
   3820  fe14							; and repositions P1 there. The per-line object path is untouched — it already
   3821  fe14							; draws from the live trio and takes COLUP1 from ObjColorTab[ObjBase+row].
   3822  fe14							;
   3823  fe14							; Invariant (do not relax): slot 1's band is STRICTLY HIGHER than slot 0's.
   3824  fe14							; Bands are set up 0->1->2, so no later band has to restore slot 0's trio.
   3825  fe14							; Rooms whose two objects share a band keep the old behaviour (slot 0 only,
   3826  fe14							; rotation in SelectActiveObject unchanged).
   3827  fe14							; Cost: the band-compare early-out sits in the setup line's free tail (0
   3828  fe14							; lines); a band that DOES host slot 1 pays 2 lines (SetObjectXPos must start
   3829  fe14							; on a line boundary and the HMOVE needs the next line's HBLANK).
